  "body": "Found while fixing #2898.\n\n## What happens\n\nA flat Circular with several rings and a helix entry gets blocking `Crossing` warnings. Verification refuses the program. The post is held. The program is refused, not unsafe.\n\nReproduce with the job of #2898, with entry `Helix` and `helix_radius` 1:\n\n- center [0,0], radius 10, tool EM-0600-4FL (25 mm flutes), stepover 2, stepdown 2\n- top Z20, bottom Z0, clearance Z30, stock_to_leave 0\n\nGeneration reports pairs such as `feed moves 2 and 84 cross in XY at shared depth`. Each pair is a helix arc of ring k-1 and a helix arc of ring k at the same level.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe Circular is ring-major: each ring runs its own level ladder, with its own entry at each level. Each helix passes through its ring's start, and its centre is one helix radius inward. When the stepover is two helix radii, the helix of ring k-1 touches the helix of ring k at the start of ring k. The two helices share one depth band. The crossing law (`crates/sim/src/verify/crossing.rs`) counts a touch as a crossing.\n\n## What was tried\n\nThe fix branch of #2898 tried the pocket's z-major order for the flat mode (all rings at one plane). That removed the crossings. But the inner rings then started with an axial plunge that was not named, also under a ramp entry. Four ramp-entry tests went red. The branch dropped that approach (`docs/decisions/2898-circular-ring-links.md`).\n\n## Expected\n\nThe helix entry of each later ring is placed so that it does not touch the helix of the ring before it, or the parameters are refused before generation with a named cause.\n\n## Workaround\n\nUse the plunge or the ramp entry, or one ring only.\n",
